# component: command
# decisions: A11Y-2, A11Y-3, A11Y-4, A11Y-7, DOC-1, DOC-2, INT-1
# hunks:
#   INT-1: `cursor-default` is removed from `CommandItem`, so a row shows the hand cursor the one
#     global rule gives every `[role="option"]`.
#   A11Y-2: `CommandInput` gains `min-h-6`. cmdk's input carries no height of its own, so it
#     measures its line box — 20px inside the 32px `InputGroup` — under the 24px target floor the
#     geometry lane probes with a real `elementFromPoint`. The same correction Batch 3 applied to
#     `ComboboxChipsInput` and the calendar's month/year dropdown. (Its focus affordance needed the
#     matching half in `input-group.tsx`: upstream names this slot `command-input`, so the group's
#     text-entry tint never saw it focus. FOC-3, recorded in `input-group.patch`.)
#   A11Y-3, A11Y-4: cmdk ships NO live region — grepping `cmdk@1.1.1`'s dist for `aria-live`
#     returns nothing — so filtering a palette to two results, or to none, is silent. `Command`
#     now renders one `useAnnouncer` region for its whole life (A11Y-4: mounted empty, keyed by a
#     sequence counter) and announces the result count politely whenever the search or the count
#     changes (A11Y-3: `role="status"`, never `alert`). It reads the count through cmdk's own
#     `useCommandState`, so the announcement is the engine's filtered total, not a second count.
#   A11Y-7 (a context-licensed role), A11Y-3: **FLAGGED FOR MK — a genuine upstream accessibility
#     defect.** A list with no options is not a listbox. cmdk hard-codes `role="listbox"` on
#     `Command.List` and `role="presentation"` on `Command.Empty`, both AFTER spreading props, so
#     neither can be overridden through JSX. An empty palette is therefore a listbox whose only
#     child is the empty message, which axe reports as a CRITICAL `aria-required-children`
#     violation (reproduced 2026-09-18: upstream's own composition fails with 1 critical; the same
#     tree with the message outside the list is clean). `CommandList` removes the role from the
#     node while `filtered.count` is 0 and restores it above 0 — which is exactly A11Y-7's rule,
#     `Item` only gets `listitem` inside `ItemGroup`, applied to the other end of the same
#     relationship — and `CommandEmpty` puts `role="status"` on the message itself (A11Y-3) so the
#     empty state is still announced. Upstream's public composition is untouched: `<CommandEmpty>`
#     still goes inside `<CommandList>`.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: prettier reflow plus the `registry-stamp.mjs` provenance header (DOC-1); no
#               decision of their own.
